Here is a complete, single-file web app (HTML + CSS + JavaScript) ready to run in any browser. 

It handles signups, tracks the remaining seats out of 20, validates inputs, prevents duplicate emails, and uses browser `localStorage` so registrations persist even if you refresh the page.

### How to use:
1. Save the code below into a file named `index.html`.
2. Double-click the file to open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Workshop Registration</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --primary: #4F46E5;
      --primary-hover: #4338CA;
      --bg: #F3F4F6;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --text: #1F2937;
      --text-muted: #6B7280;
      --border: #E5E7EB;
      --danger: #EF4444;
      --success: #10B981;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; }
    body { background-color: var(--bg); color: var(--text); display: flex; justify-content: center; padding: 2rem 1rem; min-height: 100vh; }

    .container { width: 100%; max-width: 480px; }
    .card { background: var(--card); border-radius: 12px; padding: 2rem; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.1), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.06); }

    header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }

    /* Counter badge */
    .seat-badge {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 1rem;
      padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 9999px;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      background: #EEF2FF;
      color: var(--primary);
    }
    .seat-badge.sold-out { background: #FEE2E2; color: var(--danger); }

    /* Form Styles */
    form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
    .field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; text-align: left; }
    label { font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 500; }
    input {
      padding: 0.75rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 6px;
      font-size: 1rem;
      outline: none;
      transition: border-color 0.2s;
    }
    input:focus { border-color: var(--primary); ring: 2px solid var(--primary); }

    button {
      padding: 0.75rem;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 6px;
      background: var(--primary);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: background 0.2s;
    }
    button:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--primary-hover); }
    button:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: not-allowed; }

    /* Messages */
    .alert { padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: none; }
    .alert.error { background: #FEE2E2; color: var(--danger); display: block; }
    .alert.success { background: #D1FAE5; color: #065F46; display: block; }

    /* Attendee List */
    .attendees-section { margin-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
    .attendees-section h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
    .attendee-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; max-height: 200px; overflow-y: auto; }
    .attendee-item { font-size: 0.9rem; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 0.5rem; background: var(--bg); border-radius: 4px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="card">
      <header>
        <h1>Exclusive Workshop</h1>
        <p>Join us for an intensive learning session.</p>
        <div id="seatBadge" class="seat-badge">Loading seats...</div>
      </header>

      <div id="alertBox" class="alert"></div>

      <form id="signupForm">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="name">Full Name</label>
          <input type="text" id="name" required placeholder="Jane Doe" autocomplete="name">
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="email">Email Address</label>
          <input type="email" id="email" required placeholder="jane@example.com" autocomplete="email">
        </div>
        <button type="submit" id="submitBtn">Claim Seat</button>
      </form>

      <section class="attendees-section">
        <h2>Registered Guests (<span id="count">0</span>/20)</h2>
        <ul id="attendeeList" class="attendee-list"></ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    const TOTAL_SEATS = 20;

    // Load existing attendees from localStorage, or start empty
    let attendees = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('workshop_attendees')) || [];

    // DOM Elements
    const form = document.getElementById('signupForm');
    const nameInput = document.getElementById('name');
    const emailInput = document.getElementById('email');
    const submitBtn = document.getElementById('submitBtn');
    const badge = document.getElementById('seatBadge');
    const alertBox = document.getElementById('alertBox');
    const list = document.getElementById('attendeeList');
    const countSpan = document.getElementById('count');

    function showAlert(message, type) {
      alertBox.textContent = message;
      alertBox.className = `alert ${type}`;
    }

    function hideAlert() {
      alertBox.className = 'alert';
      alertBox.textContent = '';
    }

    function updateUI() {
      const remaining = TOTAL_SEATS - attendees.length;
      countSpan.textContent = attendees.length;

      // Update badge status
      if (remaining <= 0) {
        badge.textContent = "Sold Out!";
        badge.classList.add('sold-out');
        submitBtn.disabled = true;
        nameInput.disabled = true;
        emailInput.disabled = true;
      } else {
        badge.textContent = `${remaining} seat${remaining === 1 ? '' : 's'} remaining`;
        badge.classList.remove('sold-out');
        submitBtn.disabled = false;
        nameInput.disabled = false;
        emailInput.disabled = false;
      }

      // Update attendees list preview
      list.innerHTML = '';
      attendees.forEach((att) => {
        const li = document.createElement('li');
        li.className = 'attendee-item';
        li.innerHTML = `<span>${att.name}</span> <span style="color:var(--text-muted)">${att.email}</span>`;
        list.appendChild(li);
      });
    }

    form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      hideAlert();

      const name = nameInput.value.trim();
      const email = emailInput.value.trim().toLowerCase();

      // Check capacity
      if (attendees.length >= TOTAL_SEATS) {
        showAlert("Sorry, all 20 seats are filled!", "error");
        return;
      }

      // Check duplicates
      const emailExists = attendees.some(attendee => attendee.email.toLowerCase() === email);
      if (emailExists) {
        showAlert("This email address is already registered.", "error");
        return;
      }

      // Save attendee
      attendees.push({ name, email });
      localStorage.setItem('workshop_attendees', JSON.stringify(attendees));

      // Reset and acknowledge
      nameInput.value = '';
      emailInput.value = '';
      showAlert(`Success! Seat reserved for ${name}.`, "success");

      updateUI();
    });

    // Initial render on load
    updateUI();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Features included:
* **Seat Availability Tracking:** Dynamically counts down from 20 to 0.
* **Duplicate Detection:** Prevents users from registering multiple times with the same email.
* **Local Persistence:** Data is stored in `localStorage`, meaning registrations remain saved if you refresh or close the tab.
* **Sold Out State:** Disables the form fields and buttons automatically when the 20-seat limit is reached.

